<title>MEXICO: Mexico's 27-day Cetes rate falls in auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico's 27-day Cetes rate falls in auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's 27-day Cetes rate fell in this week's primary auction and demand fell, Banco de Mexico said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent)</p>
<p>Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>27-Day	18.59	    -87	     18.50     18.74</p>
<p>91-Day	21.18	    -11	     20.73     21.24</p>
<p>182-Day     22.47	    -13	     21.99     22.75</p>
<p>342-Day     23.53				23.05     23.99</p>
<p>Last week the 349-day paper was assigned at 23.40 pct.  </p>
<p>Maturity    Assigned	  Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>27-Day	800 million pesos   1.93 bln pesos    2.41</p>
<p>91-Day	800 million pesos   2.82 bln pesos    3.52</p>
<p>182-Day     800 million pesos   1.67 bln pesos    2.09</p>
<p>342-Day     600 million pesos   1.30 bln pesos    2.17</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 2.57 on demand of 7.72 billion pesos compared to 2.98 the week before on demand of 8.95 billion pesos the week before. Tails were as follows:</p>
<p>    27-Day			   15 basis points</p>
<p>    91-Day			    6 basis points</p>
<p>    182-Day			  28 basis points</p>
<p>    342-Day			  46 basis points</p>
<p>((--Dan Trotta, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9507))</p>
</text>
